\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 7.2 The Remediation Playbook\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 \cb3 Businesses must treat this transition not as an administrative task for the legal department, but as a strategic\'a0
\f0\b Tax Health Check
\f1\b0 . The following steps are critical:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls17\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Portfolio Audit:
\f1\b0 \'a0Review every KBLI code currently registered in the NIB. Does it match the\'a0
\f2\i current
\f1\i0 \'a0revenue reality? If a code is no longer active, remove it. Unused codes are liability magnets.\cb1 \
\ls17\ilvl0
\f0\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Profitability Test:
\f1\b0 \'a0For each KBLI, consult with tax advisors to determine the DGT's "Benchmarked" profit margin. Is the company's actual margin significantly lower? If yes, prepare the "Defense File"\'a0
\f2\i now
\f1\i0 , documenting the specific commercial reasons for the lower profitability (e.g., market expansion costs, one-off write-downs) before the SP2DK arrives.\cb1 \
\ls17\ilvl0
\f0\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The "Split" Analysis:
\f1\b0 \'a0Did the company's code split in 2025? (e.g., Old "IT Services" -> New "SaaS" + "Consulting").\cb1 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls17\ilvl1
\f2\i \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Strategy:
\f1\i0 \'a0Choose the new code that best reflects the\'a0
\f2\i cost structure
\f1\i0 . If the business has high server costs, choose "Infrastructure" (Category K) rather than "Publishing" (Category J) to justify the lower margins and higher depreciation.\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls17\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Data Cleansing in Coretax:
\f1\b0 \'a0Use the Coretax portal to update the "Place of Business" and "KLU" data. Ensure the "Main KLU" (the one that determines the primary benchmark) represents the\'a0
\f2\i dominant
\f1\i0 \'a0revenue stream, not just the legacy business.\'a0\'a0\'a0\cb1 \
